      walkthrough = "**Level:** 1\n**Maximum Level:** 125\n**Monster Mission:** No\n**Repeatable:** Yes\n**Can Be Shrouded?:** No\n**Quest Type:** Task\n**Group Size:** Solo\n\nThis task is a continuation of the task Rathe Day: Softer than Otmir Fur [quest=12921]. You can get the task from Korah Kai, she is located at +1001,+1948,+32.88 in Hollowshade Moors. She's on Find (Ctrl+F).\nYou say, 'Hail, Korah Kai'\nKorah Kai smiles warmly as you greet her. She's practically bubbling over with excitement to talk with you. 'Well, if it isn't my favorite conservationist! The ursarachnids are sweet, misunderstood creatures and we can learn a lot from them. My fellow nature lovers are in the process of building a sanctuary for them so we can continue to study their behaviors.  Did you know their silk is stronger than steel and can be harvested to make armor?' She takes a moment to calm herself before continuing. 'Since you've made it this far, I'm fairly certain I can't scare you away with anything.' Her eyes grow as large as saucers. 'I want to talk to you about the [lichen] on Luclin, You do not have a choice about this now!'\nYou say, 'Lichen? As in moss?'\nKorah Kai's hands shiver as she fails to contain her joy. 'Close, but no! Moss is considered a plant, while lichen is actually a combination of a fungus and an algae. It creates a symbiotic relationship to create a different creature! Much like the owlbears and ursarachnids, except lichen can survive in some of the harshest climates due to its unique structure, which is called lichenometry. They can detect the slightest changes in their environment and adapt themselves for survival. Because of this, there are thousands of different types of lichen all over Luclin and Norrath. As an amateur lichenologist, I normally spend my free time collecting and studying this stuff, but as of late I have been [too busy].'\nYou say, 'Too busy? I can help'\nKorah Kai says, 'I know you can and that's why I love you. Did you know that some lichen is edible? I would not advise going around and consuming it without the correct knowledge, as it could kill you if you don't know what to look for. Only certain kinds are edible and such lichen can be found here on Luclin. Battle historians have said the Rallosian army would survive long marches by eating whatever they could find. Meat can be scarce and, while many starved to death, some made do with making something that they called \"bread moss.\" I understand that I just told you that it's not a \"moss,\" but this is a bit of a catchall term for the same process. It is an acquired taste and I have a friend who loves the stuff. I just need some from a very specific [location].'\nYou say, 'What kind of location are we talking?'\nKorah Kai proudly exclaims, 'The Paludal Caverns! I need you to head inside and search the caves for any living lichen you will find.' She draws a crude image of what looks like a mass of tangled webs with a mouth. 'Looks something like this. The ones that look like shrubs are called \"fruticose.\" It was there the whole time, but it's more prevalent in the caves during this time of year. Now that you know what to look for, they should be much easier to spot. Since they have absorbed the magical essence that's in the ground in that area, they react poorly to an [untrained] hand.'\nYou say, 'How can an untrained hand cause them to react differently?'\nYou have been assigned the task 'Lessons of Luclin Lichen'.\nKorah Kai cringes when you ask that question. 'Don't judge me, but it did take me a bit to understand how to collect some Luclin lichen.' She gives a worried smile. 'You gotta pat them on the side that doesn't have a mouth. I discovered it one day when I was bored and gently patted one. A piece fell off and it remained in one piece. Typically the pieces crumble to dust after a few minutes of not being attached. If you pat them, it seems to comfort the main root enough to allow a living sample to break off and survive. Look, I know that sounds crazy, but I don't make the rules. Nature does! Go gather me some lichen from the Paludal Caverns, Kenadi.'\nKorah Is happy you have relumed from your work with Reeve Purewing and the ursarachnids. She was afraid of you being too afraid to continue. Having proved her wrong, she has one more task to fully tell you about the Importance of conservation. This time, however, it is no beast you hunt but a type of creature that is a combination of algae and fungus, lichen.\nKorah has asked that you head into the Paludal Caverns and retrieve some lichen for her. She warns you that with the peculiar structure of the Paludal Caverns lichen, you will have to pat them in order to collect a piece that won't crumble immediately.\n- 1. Collect lichen from the Paludal Caverns 0/1 Paludal Caverns\nLook for living Luclin lichen creatures not far from the Shadeweaver's Thicket zoneline near the big pool of water.\nTarget them and /pat them. You are given Paludal Lichen.\n- 2. Deliver the Paludal Caverns lichen to Korah Kai 0/1 Hollowshade Moor\nYou offered 1 Paludal Lichen to Korah Kai.\nYou have been given: Paludal Bread Moss Loaf\nYour task 'Lessons of Luclin Lichen' has been updated.\nKorah Kai  looks pleased with what you brought her, as she gently wraps it in some paper and stuffs it in a shirt pocket. She reaches into a pouch and pulls out a cloth-covered cube. She removes the cloth to show a steaming loaf of bread that has intricate designs cut and baked into the top of it. She wraps it back up and hands it to you. 'When you left, I remembered that I had extra stashed away just for this very reason. I thank you for replenishing my stock. Take this loaf to Tarka in the Cobalt Scar. You will find him at his favorite fishing spot. You may be asking yourself if this tastes any good. I'm happy to tell you that, when prepared correctly, no.'\nYou complete the trade with Korah Kai.\n- 3. Bring the Bread Moss Loaf to Tarka 0/1 Cobalt Scar\nHunter Tarka is in Cobalt Scar at /way -714, -199, 59 along the beach between the druid ring portal and skyshrine.\nYou offered 1 Paludal Bread Moss Loaf to Hunter Tarka.\nYou have been given: Tarka's Old Tacklebox\nYour task 'Lessons of Luclin Lichen' has been updated.\nHunter Tarka happily takes the loaf of bread from you. He unwraps the cloth from around the loaf and inhales deeply. A waft of the loaf's scent enters your nostrils and assaults your senses. It smells like a hot swamp was baked into a loaf of seaweed. Tarka smiles devilishly and wraps the loaf in the towel before storing it in a pouch on his side. 'Just like how mom made it when I was just a pup. She was a traveling merchant and she would collect lichen from the Paludal Caverns. She would bake a loaf every time she came home. She liked keeping old traditions alive by recreating them without the modern tools. I haven't smelled this smell in a long time. Oh, please bring [this] to Korah.'\nYou complete the trade with Hunter Tarka.\n- 4. Return to Korah and give her the tacklebox 0/1 Hollowshade Moor\nYou offered 1 Tarka's Old Tacklebox to Korah Kai.\nYour task 'Lessons of Luclin Lichen' has been updated.\nKorah Kai takes the tacklebox and looks at it confused. She looks at you, then back to the tacklebox. You can almost see the clockwork moving in her head. 'Oh! Tarka, you genius! This is a great idea!' She stops herself quickly and places a hand on her chest as she addresses you, 'Gebb, as always, thank you.' She does an excited little dance before regaining her composure. 'Tarka and I are close and have been for a long time. I consider him a dear friend. I thank you for this, Gebb! Did you know that lichen is also used for making an assortment of dyes? With that being said, you know what I'm going to ask next.' She smiles warmly. 'I need you to gear up and get into Velketor's Labyrinth. The neat thing about the lichen you will find there is that it is very resilient to the cold and is quite sturdy. If you can't collect it from the source, ask around. Someone may have some extra.' She gives you a wink as you go on your way.\nYou complete the trade with Korah Kai.\n- 5. Find lichen grown from within Velketor's Labyrinth 0/1 ALL\nYou can find the lichen not far from the Great Divide zoneline. Same thing, target them and /pat\nYou pat a living Velious lichen on the back.\nYour task 'Lessons of Luclin Lichen' has been updated.\nYou are given: Velketor's Lichen\n- 6. Give the lichen to Korah Kai 0/1 Hollowshade Moor\nYou offered 1 Velketor's Lichen to Korah Kai.\nYou have been given: Velketor's Dye\nYour task 'Lessons of Luclin Lichen' has been updated.\nKorah Kai sees you approach and she removes a mortar and pestle from her pouch. She kneels down and places the mortar on the ground and removes a few vials from her coat pocket, pops the cork on them and pours them into the mortar. She takes the lichen, placing it in the mortar, and begins to crush it with the pestle. While she is preparing whatever she is preparing, she looks up to speak to you. 'Thank you for this. Yet again I am in your debt and you have made my life a little bit easier.' She's getting winded and stops talking to focus on her work. Once finished, she wipes the sweat from her forehead using the back of her hand before setting down the pestle and pouring the contents of the mortar into an envelope she pulled from her coat. She hands you the [envelope].\nYou complete the trade with Korah Kai.\n- 7. Bring the envelope of dye to Guard Kroffa 0/1 South Kaladim\nGuard Kroffa is just inside the zone from ButcherBlock Mountains. Give him the dye.\nYou offered 1 Velketor's Dye to Guard Kroffa.\nYou have been given: Bag of Butcherblock Samples\nYour task 'Lessons of Luclin Lichen' has been updated.\nGuard Kroffa takes the envelope from you and quickly hides it in his armor. 'Ye daft? I din't need tha others ta know I'm out of dye for me drawers!' He reaches for a heavy sack that has a bunch of pockets in it and hands it to you. 'Aye, this be the sack she be wantin'. Filled ta the brim with all o' tha dirt and plants I could find. She kept goin' oon about protecting the land 'n whatever. I din't listen too close. Bring this ta her. Careful, my friend. She'll talk ya ear off about tha stuff if ya let her.'\nYou complete the trade with Guard Kroffa.\n- 8. Deliver the sample to Korah 0/1 Hollowshade Moor\nYou offered 1 Bag of Butcherblock Samples to Korah Kai.\nYour task 'Lessons of Luclin Lichen' has been updated.\nKorah Kai excitedly takes the pouch with a flourish and a twirl. 'Thank you, Gebb! As I have promised, I have no more tasks for you. Though what you have done for me today feels like a pile of chores, but I think I'm going to continue doing this every year. Make it an event, you know? Every time the owlbears migrate, we reflect upon our lands and do something to help out Norrath. Maybe call it Rathe Day? Tell you what, I declare to you and all of my lichen samples that, come this time next migration, I will have finished that sanctuary! Thank you for everything yet again, Gebb. I'll see you next year.'\nYou complete the trade with Korah Kai.\n- 9. Speak with the Rathe Initiate 0/1 Plane of Knowledge\na Rathe Initiate can be found at /way -39, -74, -156 not far from the Crescent Reach stone.\nYou say, 'Hail, a Rathe Initiate'\nYour task 'Lessons of Luclin Lichen' has been updated.\nWhether you lichened it or not, you did learn the importance of such diverse and incredible creatures. Your actions on this day have shown the Rathe Council can trust you to grasp the importance of conservation. They have deemed this day \"Rathe Day\" in hopes that creating the tradition of conservation will encourage future generations of explorers to take care of the planet they live on.\nYou have been given: Living Lump of Luclin Lichen\nA Rathe Initiate greets you with a slight bow of respect. 'I welcome your return, adventurer. I thank you for partaking in those tasks for her.' They pause as they scratch what you think is their chin under the mask. 'Rathe Day, huh? We do enjoy the way that sounds. I will return in one year's time to check on Korah's status. It will be interesting to see if you mortals will actually take protecting these lands seriously. Of course it would be easier to do all of this with magicks, but that is just using energy from one ecosystem for another. That is not the lesson we wish to teach here. Doing the work is worth it. We are glad you understand, Gebb. Thank you again. Until next year, my friend.'\nYou have completed achievement: Rathe Day: Rathe Day Reveler\nReward(s):\nLiving Lump of Luclin Lichen (Pet Illusion or Familiar)\nSubmitted by: GidonoRewards:\n- Living Lump of Luclin Lichen [item=149037]\n[",
